# Lesson 5, new exercise: a weak hand with long diamonds over 1NT.
title: Weak with six diamonds
id: L05-12
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.1
student: S
board: 24
dealer: W
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AQ98   87     KQ92   KJ8
  E  KJ43   QT95   J      A653
  S  52     J6     AT8654 972
  W  T76    AK432  73     QT4

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2D*    = To play: fewer than 8 points, long diamonds
     key: A weak hand with six diamonds: bid 2♦, and partner must pass.
     not Pass: Your hand is worth little in no-trump, but several tricks in diamonds.
     not 2C: Stayman shows 8+ points and a major. You have neither.
  W Pass
  N Pass   = 2♦ is to play
  E Pass

auction recap:
  With 5 points and six diamonds, your hand is weak in no-trump but useful
  with diamonds as trumps. 2♦ asks partner to pass, and he does. You are
  declarer, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 3
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W HA  N H7  E H5  S H6
  2   W HK  N H8  E H9  S HJ
  3   W ST  N S8  E S3  S S2
  4   W H4  N D2*  E HT  S C2
      D2 key: Ruff: dummy is out of hearts.
      D2 not CK: Did you notice dummy has no hearts left? Ruff instead of letting the heart win.
      D2 not SA: Did you notice dummy has no hearts left? Ruff instead of letting the heart win.
      note: Dummy ruffs.
  5   N DK*  E DJ  S D4  W D3
      DK key: Now draw trumps.
      DK not SA: Did you remember to draw trumps before cashing your side winners?
      DK not CK: Did you remember to draw trumps before cashing your side winners?
      note: Draw trumps.
  6   N DQ  E C3  S D5  W D7
      note: Trumps are drawn.
  7   N SA  E S4  S S5  W S6
      note: Trumps are drawn. Take the ace of spades.
      ok: C
  8   N SQ  E SJ  S C7  W S7
      note: Cash the queen of spades too.
      ok: C
  9   N CK  E CA  S C9  W C4
      note: Lead a club to knock out the ace.
  10  E SK  S D6  W H2  N S9
      note: You ruff.
  11  S DA  W H3  N D9  E C5
      note: Cash your trump winners.
  12  S DT  W CT  N C8  E C6
      note: Keep cashing trumps.
  13  S D8  W CQ  N CJ  E HQ
      note: 9 tricks: 2♦ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  The plan: ruff the third heart in dummy, draw trumps, then cash your
  winners. Ruffing first stops West's heart winner; drawing trumps next
  keeps the defense from ruffing yours.

  2♦ made nine tricks. 1NT would have made too, just, with seven. Most of
  the time a hand like yours takes more tricks with diamonds as trumps than
  it adds in no-trump, so 2♦ is the safer bet.
